From 8e883a898ea1bdc3d17b9151b006e3772a9dada6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:08:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 44/57] hw/misc: mikroBUS AN and UART; the POT Click

Sockets gain the analog pin AN (a Click's analog output, in millivolts,
set on the ADC channels behind the pad) and a UART (a UART Click is a
chardev the board connects to the socket's UART before realizing the
MCU, linked as /machine/<socket>-click). The MC00 Curiosity Pro wires AN
to ADC0/ADC1 and both headers' shared SERCOM3; the AVR64EA48 Nano Base
sockets 1 and 3 share USART2. First user: the POT Click (click-pot), a
potentiometer on an MCP1501 2.048 V reference buffered onto AN.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
